Ringsmith ER-026 (from ER-014; ruling LuciDin 18 Nov 2026, docs/decomp_recipes.md 3.4)

ee-as for the r5900: no FP condition-code hazard nop between c.cond.s and bc1t / bc1f when the branch is
assembled in reorder mode (gcc left the delay slot empty). In .set noreorder blocks the nop stays.
Reproduces the game's 129 reorder sites and keeps its 1,069 noreorder ones. A documented reconstruction of
Sony's assembler behaviour, not Sony's code (docs/toolchain.md 4.4).

Applies to SSXModding/ps2-ee-toolchain b595ded, directory ee/ (patch -p1 -d <src>/ee).

--- a/gas/config/tc-mips.c
+++ b/gas/config/tc-mips.c
@@ -1511,7 +1511,8 @@
       else if (! mips_opts.mips16
 	       && mips_opts.isa < 4
 	       && (prev_pinfo & INSN_WRITE_COND_CODE)
-               && ! cop_interlocks)
+               && ! cop_interlocks
+	       && ! (mips_cpu == 5900 && ! mips_opts.noreorder)) /* Ringsmith ER-014/ER-026 */
 	{
 	  /* The previous instruction sets the coprocessor condition
 	     codes, but does not require a general coprocessor delay
